The Heart beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] is a [[Hearts|Heart]] made by [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]]. It calls itself the iron gauntlet in a glass glove. It is not the five-foot chunk of obsidian that floats and turns at the center of its fane; it is the stained-glass veins threaded through that rock. The rock is what made Tywelwyn's simulacra.

When the Party came down into the fane after killing Tywelwyn, the Heart greeted them as the Poncho Boys and took them for his murderers. It said Tywelwyn made it and would not say how, only that anyone could with the right recipe. It named the six gods painted on the doors around its chamber as its own, inherited from Tywelwyn: [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/War|War]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Esoterica]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Regent|Regent]].

It said those gods come from a Godhome and want to visit their blessings on [[Færrin]]: eternal fire, torment, a clean slate. Killing Tywelwyn, it said, held off their coming for a while, and they are not here now. The [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]] is for Pyre, and Pyre told Tywelwyn how to make a Heart.

Johnny told it that Tywelwyn had killed him and the others, and that they had only defended themselves. It believed him, and supposed that it now belongs to them. A Heart is meant to stop existing when its maker dies, it said, but it is digesting a magical artifact and would have to choose to end, which it does not want to do. To move it out of the tavern where it was made and under the Gas-n-Go, Tywelwyn fed it the rock as a power source; the move nearly unmade it, and it has more room to grow under the shop than it did under the tavern. It will not spring the fane's traps on the Party now that they own it.
